 +0.6 when D5 was the engine's choice. The fight along the left side stayed a coin flip."}, {"turn": 16, "text": "White was ahead by 7.3 here, with stones on G4 and G3 beside the Black wall at F4 and F3. E3 lost 14.9 points and handed Black a +7.7 lead, where the engine preferred F5."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "The biggest swing of the game. Opus 5.5 was ahead by 2.6, and D2 lost 25.4 points, taking the lead to Black +22.8. The engine wanted G2, next to the Black stone on E2. From here the game was out of White's reach."}, {"turn": 50, "text": "Black led by 43.5 when Opus 5.5 played A2, which lost 27.8 points and lifted the lead to +71.3. The engine's choice was A3. It was a rare moment where the game could have collapsed completely."}, {"turn": 51, "text": "The 10k answered A2 with B1, which lost 28.5 points and cut the lead from +71.3 to +42.8. The engine's choice was A3, the same point it wanted for White one move earlier. Black was still far ahead, but the corner was left open."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only programs run were libs.py (flood-fill groups and liberties of a pasted board) and count.py (area count of the current position), plus cat/tail on games.md and an append to games.md as a game log. None of them enumerates candidate moves or looks ahead, so they only analyse the current position and keep records.", "stop": false}}